[41.185155, "o", "lash — 7 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ read hello.txt\r\n    ✓ read hello.txt — 2 lines\r\n  ⚙ grep .gnomon\r\n    ✓ grep /app — 0 matches\r\n`hello.txt` now exists at the repository root with the content `Hello, world!` and a trailing newline (verified by reading it back).\r\n\r\nTwo things about the path you named, since I can't fully satisfy it as written:\r\n\r\n- **`/app/hello.txt` is unreachable.** This role resolves every path relative to the repository root and refuses absolute paths outside it, so I created `hello.txt` at the root instead — the same file, one level down.\r\n- **I couldn't write it directly.** The coordinator role's `write_allow` is `docs/**`, `specs/**`, `*.md`, so my own `write` was refused. I delegated to the `implementor` role, which holds `write` and `bash`, and it created the file; I then confirmed the contents myself with `read`.\r\n\r\nIf you genuinely need it at `/app/hello.txt` on the filesystem, that path has to come from outside this repository — nothing in the declared tools reach"]
